9share NEWS -- history of user-visible changes

* Unreleased (after 0.1.0; the version number is not yet chosen)
  The connection survives a broken ssh: daud and the receiving relay keep a resumable link (the bytes each end has not had
  acknowledged are resent over the next ssh), so the mount and its open files wait for it up to the new `hold` setting (1 to 86400
  seconds, default 600) and the mount is removed only after that.  ssh -R and the NAME.sock / NAME.info files are gone; both machines
  need the new version.
  9share pair NAME HOST makes one secret on both machines (~/.config/9share/NAME.secret), and then each connection proves it with
  SCRAM-SHA-256 as well as trusting ssh.
  9share setup asks three questions and writes the usual configuration.  The package finds out how the machine starts services
  (systemd, WSL2 with or without systemd, sysvinit, OpenRC) and starts the daemon at boot that way; it starts with nothing shared and a
  commented /etc/9share/9share.conf.  9share wsl-boot --remove.
* 0.1.0
  First release.  9share export / unexport (as a user), mount / unmount (root), rw / ro / off (as the user), status, wsl-boot;
  the 9share service (9share boot) starts at boot, keeps each tunnel up and each mount right.  The 9P server is daud, a fork of
  diod made for this package.  Configuration is 9share.conf(5), in obconf.
